<title>GERMANY: Pan-German final Dec cpi inflation +1.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pan-German final Dec cpi inflation +1.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN CPI INFLATION		 Dec 96	Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.3	  -0.1	 +0.3</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.4	  +1.4	 +1.8</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    117.0	 116.7	115.4</p>
<p> FINAL WEST GERMAN CPI INFLATION  Dec 96	Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.3	  -0.1	 +0.3</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.4	  +1.4	 +1.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    114.6	 114.3	113.0</p>
<p> EAST GERMAN CPI INFLATION	 Dec 96	 Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.1	  +0.1	 +0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year			    +1.6	  +1.6	 +2.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    136.0	 135.9	133.9</p>
<p>NOTE - The office said consumer price inflation in 1996 averaged 1.5 percent in all Germany, 1.4 percent in west Germany and 2.2 percent in east Germany.  </p>
<p>The Office gave the following details:</p>
<p>					    Mth/mth	     Yr/yr</p>
<p>					Dec 96  Nov 96    Dec 96  Nov 96</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco	     +0.1    +0.4	+1.1    +1.1</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes		    unch    +0.2	+0.8    +0.8</p>
<p> Rents &amp; energy		     +0.2    unch	+2.1    +2.2</p>
<p> Of which: rents		    +0.2    +0.2	+2.7    +2.7</p>
<p>	     energy excl. fuel    +0.5    -0.9	-0.1    -0.1</p>
<p> Furniture, household goods     unch    +0.1	+0.6    +0.6</p>
<p> Health and body care goods     unch    +0.2	+2.1    +2.1</p>
<p> Traffic and news transmission  -0.1    -0.1	+1.6    +2.0</p>
<p> Education, leisure goods	 +0.3    unch	+0.7    +0.6</p>
<p> Personal equipment, others     +2.2    -2.2	+1.2    +0.3</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
